- [x] Delivered OTP & passwordless  -> Module 11 (11-otp-passwordless)
      Gap found: the course had TOTP (Module 3) but nothing on the OTP the server
      *sends* — email/SMS codes and magic links — which is the most deployed
      factor in the world and a different threat model entirely.
      Built: Go+Redis+Mailpit passwordless service. Email/SMS OTP with attempt cap
      + burn, short TTL, single use, peppered HMAC over requestID||code (a 6-digit
      code is 20 bits — password-style hashing is useless), CSPRNG codes,
      constant-time compare, uniform anti-enumeration responses, per-identifier AND
      per-source send quotas, resend that invalidates the prior code. Magic links
      with atomic DEL single-use + same-browser cookie binding. MODE=unsafe (+
      OTP_DIGITS=4) reruns the same demos as successful attacks: brute force,
      OTP bombing, SMS toll fraud with a simulated telecom bill on /metrics.
      All four demo scripts run green in safe mode and break as intended unsafe.
